  "agent_descriptions": [],
  "final": "The test suite passes now. All 7 tests are green, and the 183 failures came from a single bug.\n\nThe bug was in `reorder_qty` in `inventory/stock.py`. It used floor division (`need // pack_size`), so it rounded down to whole packs. Its docstring and `test_reorder_rounds_up_to_whole_pack` both expect it to round up. Each of the 199 `need` values in that test is its own subtest, so the output was huge. 183 of them failed, and each one printed its own traceback.\n\nI changed it to ceiling division, `-(-need // pack_size)`. I didn't touch the tests or `logutil`.",
